From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:31:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/display: hdmi: Force a modeset when the FRL configuration
 changes

drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_check() forces a modeset when the
output color depth, format or RGB quantization range changes, but not
when the FRL configuration does. That one can change on its own, with
the same mode, depth and format, when the sink's EDID changes its
maximum TMDS character rate or FRL rate (an EDID override, or another
sink on the connector). Without a modeset the commit leaves the link
running with the old configuration, while the connector state
describes the new one.

Treat a change of the FRL rate or lane count like a change of the
color depth and set mode_changed on the CRTC.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
index 41dcd8b1511f..14e4e9e29fb3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
@@ -977,7 +977,9 @@ int drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
 
 	if (old_conn_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb != new_conn_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb ||
 	    old_conn_state->hdmi.output_bpc != new_conn_state->hdmi.output_bpc ||
-	    old_conn_state->hdmi.output_format != new_conn_state->hdmi.output_format) {
+	    old_conn_state->hdmi.output_format != new_conn_state->hdmi.output_format ||
+	    old_conn_state->hdmi.frl_rate_per_lane != new_conn_state->hdmi.frl_rate_per_lane ||
+	    old_conn_state->hdmi.frl_lanes != new_conn_state->hdmi.frl_lanes) {
 		struct drm_crtc *crtc = new_conn_state->crtc;
 		struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state;
 
